# Full-resolution masters. The web-optimised derivatives beside them are the
# committed assets; keeping the multi-megabyte originals out of history keeps
# clones small (git history is permanent, so they can't be pruned later).
assets/bg1.png

# macOS AppleDouble sidecars. The repo lives on an exFAT volume, which cannot
# store extended attributes natively, so the OS writes a ._<name> file beside
# every file it touches. They are not source and must never be committed.
._*
